[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m To maximize this expression, we can use the method of finding the maximum value of a linear combination of sine and cosine functions. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m Let's calculate this using Python.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m b = -432
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m # Maximum value of the expression
