[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\). Then, we can express the given expression in terms of \(\theta\):
