[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\), where \(\theta\) is a real number. This means that \(z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 4(75 + 117i)e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}e^{-i\theta} = 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m Expanding this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 4(75\cos\theta + 117i\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{96\cos\theta - 144i\cos\theta + 96i\sin\theta + 144\sin\theta}{4}.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m Combining real and imaginary parts, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(4 \cdot 117\cos\theta + 4 \cdot 75\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta - i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m The real part of this expression is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=205289)[0m \[
